{"scenario": {"window_size": "1440x900", "gh": "../fixtures/gh/pr_threads.json", "description": "GitHub's threads on a pull request's review (PLAN §9.6, §9.12 step 3; DESIGN §4.5) against a fixture GitHub and mock_gh: pull request 7 opens with six threads of GitHub's, an open one with a reply placed exactly where GitHub has it, one on the whole file, a resolved one (collapsed), one GitHub calls outdated, made on a commit the review doesn't show (the \"Not in the diff\" section, with its diff hunk), the viewer's own pending one, and one whose diff hunk shows other code than its line holds, which dv can't place (the section too, \"Can't be placed\"); they are in `session.github_threads` and the comments list's \"On GitHub\" group, counted apart in the status bar, read by the CLI with `gh:` keys, and none is in the review's log; `]` steps through them, `R` on one says that replying arrives with submitting and the `X` after it only takes that notice away, `X` on one GitHub doesn't let the viewer resolve says so, Open on GitHub and Copy as prompt go through the system seam, the prompt quoting each comment under a heading of GitHub's own; Resolve sends `resolveReviewThread` (the gh log has the mutation with the thread's id) and the refresh after it shows the thread resolved; a Resolve GitHub refuses leaves the card as it was with why, which a refresh doesn't take away; a push and a refresh move the draft and its GitHub threads with it; then the review is closed, the pull request moves on again, and the threads GitHub has at the new head relocate into the head the closed review still shows, where Unresolve still works, since it is GitHub's state."}}
{"cmd": "wait_ready", "timeout_ms": 20000}
{"cmd": "set_setting", "key": "mode", "value": "dark"}
{"cmd": "settle"}

// The fixture GitHub: dv-fixture/api with pull request 7, one commit adding src/lib.rs.
{"cmd": "seed_repo", "name": "api", "github": [{"branch": "feat"}, {"checkout": "feat"}, {"write": "src/lib.rs", "text": "pub fn answer() -> u32 {\n    42\n}\n\npub fn question() -> &'static str {\n    \"what?\"\n}\n"}, {"commit": "Add the answer"}, {"pr": [7, "feat"]}], "save": {"head": "/github/prs/7"}, "expect_result": {"pointer": "/github/prs/7", "equals": "fdd652adef6c3a595882996fdf54e7741422d693"}}
{"cmd": "open_pr", "path": "${data_dir}/repos/api", "pr": "#7", "save": {"review": "/review_id"}, "expect_result": {"pointer": "/created", "equals": true}}
{"cmd": "wait_for", "pointer": "/session/github_threads", "len": 6, "timeout_ms": 20000}
{"cmd": "settle", "timeout_ms": 20000, "expect": [{"pointer": "/shell/banner", "equals": null}, {"pointer": "/session/status", "equals": "draft"}, {"pointer": "/session/pr/stale", "equals": null}, {"pointer": "/session/pr/mirror/threads", "equals": 6}, {"pointer": "/session/threads", "len": 0}]}

